====Noun====
{{en-noun}}
[[Image:Comb.png|thumb|right|A comb for the hair.]]

# A toothed implement:
## A toothed implement for grooming the hair or (formerly) for keeping it in place.
##* {{RQ:Christie Autobiography|II|4|passage=There was also hairdressing: hairdressing, too, really was hairdressing in those times — no running a '''comb''' through it and that was that. It was curled, frizzed, waved, put in curlers overnight, waved with hot tongs;{{nb...}}.}}
## A machine used in separating choice cotton fibers from worsted cloth fibers.
## The toothed plate at the top and bottom of an [[escalator]] that prevents objects getting trapped between the moving stairs and fixed landings.
## A toothed tool used for chasing screws on work in a [[lathe]]; a [[chaser]].
## The notched [[scale]] of a [[wire]] [[micrometer]].
## The [[collector]] of an electrical machine, usually resembling a comb.
## A toothed plate used for creating wells in agar gels for electrophoresis.
## {{lb|en|weaving}} A toothed wooden pick used to push the [[weft]] thread tightly against the previous pass of thread to create a tight weave.
## One of a pair of peculiar [[organ]]s on the base of the [[abdomen]] in [[scorpion]]s, with which they comb substrate.
# A crest:
## A fleshy growth on the top of the head of some birds and reptiles; [[crest]].
## {{lb|en|by extension}} A [[crest]] (of metal, leather, etc) on a piece of [[armor]], especially on a helmet.
##* {{quote-journal|en|year=1888|journal=United Service Institution of India|title=Journal of the United Service Institution of India|page=197
|passage=The head-dress of the Horse Grenadiers consists of a peculiar leather helmet with a '''comb''' of bear&#39;s skin passing over it from ear to ear and a long scarlet&nbsp;{{...}}}}
##* {{quote-text|en|year=1898|author=John Starkie Gardner|title=Armour in England from the Earliest Times to the Seventeenth Century|page=44
|passage=The armet has usually a low central cabled '''comb''' with parallel flutes on either side, occasionally there are three or five '''combs'''.}}
##* {{quote-text|en|year=1909|author=Albert Frederick Calvert|title=Madrid: An Historical Description and Handbook of the Spanish Capital|page=82
|passage=The '''combs''' or elbow pieces are beautifully made, and over the right armpit is {{...}}}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2021|author=Charles Henry Ashdown|title=British and Foreign Arms & Armour|publisher=Good Press
|passage=Charles I. (Edinburgh Castle) The Pikeman of the time of James I. was accoutred in a morion-shaped helmet with a '''comb''' of moderate size and a flat brim,&nbsp;{{...}}}}
## The top part of a gun’s stock.
# A structure of hexagon cells made by bees for storing honey; [[honeycomb]].
#* {{quote-book|en|title=[[:s:Sikhim and Bhutan|Sikhim and Bhutan]]|author=John Claude White|year=1909|page=9
|passage=The '''combs''' of the wild bees are found on overhanging precipices, and the only means by which they can be reached is to descend from above on narrow cane ladders just wide enough for a man’s foot, and often 300 feet to 400 feet long.}}
# {{lb|en|music}} The main body of a [[harmonica]] containing the air chambers and to which the [[reed plate]]s are attached.
# A [[former]]<!--noun: that which forms-->, commonly cone-shaped, used in [[hat]] manufacturing for hardening soft fibre.
# An old English measure of corn equal to the half [[quarter]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1882|author=James Edwin {{w|Thorold Rogers}}|title=A History of Agriculture and Prices in England|volume=4|page=207
|url=https://archive.org/stream/historyofagricul04rogeuoft#page/n7/mode/2up
|passage=But the '''comb''' or half quarter is very general in the Eastern counties, particularly in Norfolk.}}
# The curling crest of a wave; a [[comber]].
# {{label|en|algebraic geometry}} A [[connected]] and [[reduced]] [[curve]] with [[irreducible]] components consisting of a [[smooth]] [[subcurve]] (called the [[handle]]) and one or more additional irreducible components (called [[tooth|teeth]]) that each [[intersect]] the handle in a single [[point]] that is [[unequal]] to the [[unique]] point of [[intersection]] for any of the other teeth.
# {{lb|en|Cornwall|mining|obsolete}} A kind of [[vertical]] [[plate]] in a [[lode]].

