====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|especially of hair or fur}} To [[groom]] with a [[toothed]] [[implement]], especially a [[#Noun|comb]].
#: {{ux|en|I need to '''comb''' my hair before we leave the house.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[separate]] [[choice]] [[cotton]] [[fiber]]s from [[worsted]] [[cloth]] fibers.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[search]] [[thoroughly]] as if [[rake|raking]] over an area with a [[#Noun|comb]].
#: {{ux|en|Police '''combed''' the field for evidence after the assault.}}
# {{lb|en|nautical|intransitive}} To [[roll]] over, as the [[top]] or [[crest]] of a [[wave]]; to [[break]] with a [[white]] [[foam]], as waves.
# {{lb|en|naval|transitive}} To [[turn]] a [[vessel]] [[parallel]] to (the [[track]] of) (a [[torpedo]]) so as to [[reduce]] one's [[size]] as a [[target]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2010|author=Jim Crossley|title=Bismarck: The Epic Chase
|passage=The aircraft split up so as to attack from different, preselected bearings, thus confusing the gunners and making it difficult for the ship to '''comb''' torpedo tracks.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2013|author=Steve Backer|title=British Battlecruisers of the Second World War|page=10
|passage=Sixteen torpedo bombers divided their attention between the two ships. ''Repulse'' '''combed''' the torpedo wakes and knocked down two of the attackers.}}

